---
// Product page: Sessions, 1:1 from design/Product Pages.dc.html (tab 0).
// Dataset carried verbatim from the composite's DCLogic script per the
// founder's fidelity ruling: the aspirational metrics and CLI example
// (< 100 ms, < 90 s, 4,000 kills, 41 MB, 1.2 GB, restored in 87s) are
// design content now. The gate tags G-101/G-102/G-107 link to /proof.
import Product from './_Product.astro';

const metrics = [
  { label: 'Warm resume', value: '< 100 ms', note: 'same host, 1,000 trials', badge: 'MEASURED' as const },
  { label: 'Cold resume', value: '< 90 s', note: 'cross-region, p95', badge: 'MEASURED' as const },
  { label: 'Bytes lost across a kill', value: '0', note: '4,000 kills, claude-code', badge: 'MEASURED' as const },
];
---
<Product
  slug="sessions"
  title="Sessions · KeepState"
  description="Your agent runs inside a micro-VM KeepState can freeze whole: filesystem, model memory, and tool state captured as one atomic snapshot."
  eyebrow="Sessions"
  headline="Kill it anywhere. Resume anywhere."
  standfirst="Your agent runs inside a micro-VM we can freeze whole. Filesystem, model memory, and tool state are captured as one atomic snapshot, so the world it wakes into and the world it remembers are the same world."
  metrics={metrics}
  evidenceLine="Resume latency and durability are gated on every release; the raw output is public."
  gateTag="G-101, G-102, G-107"
  ctaHead="Pull the plug on your own agent."
  ctaBody="Free credits cover a six-hour run and the kill that would have ended it."
>
  <div class="grid gap-11 items-start grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,320px),1fr))]">
    <div>
      <div class="flex items-stretch gap-2.5">
        <div class="flex-[1_1_84px] min-w-0 bg-white border border-sand rounded-4 px-3 py-[18px] text-center">
          <p class="font-mono text-12 text-ink m-0">filesystem</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex-none flex items-center font-mono text-16 text-mist">+</div>
        <div class="flex-[1_1_84px] min-w-0 bg-white border border-sand rounded-4 px-3 py-[18px] text-center">
          <p class="font-mono text-12 text-ink m-0">KV cache</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex-none flex items-center font-mono text-16 text-mist">+</div>
        <div class="flex-[1_1_84px] min-w-0 bg-white border border-sand rounded-4 px-3 py-[18px] text-center">
          <p class="font-mono text-12 text-ink m-0">tool state</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex justify-center py-3.5">
        <span class="block w-px h-[34px] bg-sand"></span>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-blushBg border border-shell rounded-4 p-[22px] flex items-center justify-center gap-3">
        <span class="w-[9px] h-[9px] bg-claret rotate-45 block"></span>
        <p class="font-mono text-14 text-claret m-0">one atomic checkpoint</p>
      </div>
      <p class="text-14 leading-[1.6] text-slate mt-4 mb-0">Kill it anywhere. Resume anywhere. The world and the memory can never disagree.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="text-16 leading-[1.75] text-slate m-0 mb-5">A session is a micro-VM we can freeze. The freeze is one write, not three: if the filesystem were captured at t and the model memory at t plus 40 ms, the agent would wake remembering a file that does not exist.</p>
      <p class="text-16 leading-[1.75] text-slate m-0 mb-6">Storage is content-addressed, so checkpointing every five minutes costs about 41 MB per freeze rather than a fresh 1.2 GB. That is why the cadence can be aggressive enough to make a crash boring.</p>
      <div class="bg-ink rounded-5 px-[18px] py-4">
        <pre class="font-mono text-[12.5px] leading-[1.8] text-parchment m-0 overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre">$ ks run --image claude-code --checkpoint 5m
<span class="text-termMuted">session s_7f3a started</span>
$ kill -9 14203
$ ks resume s_7f3a
<span class="text-blush">restored in 87s · nonce match · 0 bytes lost</span><span class="inline-block w-[7px] h-3 bg-blush align-[-2px] ml-1 [animation:ksBlink_1s_step-end_infinite]"></span></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Product>
